        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(sync): add quiet presence mode",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Add `wacli sync --presence-mode normal|quiet`, defaulting to `normal`.\n- Preserve current sync presence behaviour by default.\n- In `quiet` mode, suppress available presence on connect and push-name updates while still sending unavailable presence on cleanup.\n- Document the personal mirror use case and add presence-mode tests.\n\n## Why\n\nLong-running `sync --follow` sessions can keep the linked device globally available. For personal-number mirror deployments, that can interfere with primary phone notification behaviour. Quiet mode gives operators an explicit opt-in that avoids available-presence updates without weakening the existing cleanup safety.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `CGO_ENABLED=1 CGO_CFLAGS=\"-Wno-error=missing-braces\" go test -tags sqlite_fts5 ./internal/app ./cmd/wacli`\n- `pnpm format:check && pnpm lint && pnpm test && pnpm build` in an unprivileged copy at `/tmp/wacli-gate`\n\nNote: the same full gate fails when run as root in `/root/clawd/repos/wacli` because `internal/fsutil` correctly expects chmod `0500` to be non-writable, but root can still write. The unprivileged run passes.\n\nCloses #297\n",
